<title>JAPAN: CADES launches 100 bln yen 5.2% yen/dlr samurai.</title>
<headline>CADES launches 100 bln yen 5.2% yen/dlr samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai issue was announced by one of the joint lead managers, Nikko Securities, on Monday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Caisse d'Amortissement de la Dette Sociale</p>
<p>			(CADES)</p>
<p> AMT		 100 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.2 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  27 April 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  28 April 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 14 to April 25</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGERS   Nikko Securities and Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,030.31 for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
